+# Synthetic stdlib retirement inventory
+
+Per-package retirement inventory for the graalgo synthetic stdlib
+packages (REVIEW-2026-11-07-22 F1/F2, lane rev1107-22-f1).
+Companion to the bridge inventory
+([bridge-inventory.md](bridge-inventory.md) B-4) and to the
+`stdlib-linkdiff` v2.0.0 change in the same lane: the tool no longer
+credits synthetic packages, so its skip-list is now the honest
+worklist, and this file is the per-package side of that worklist —
+one row per synthetic package, with the root-cause fix that retires it
+once that fix is known.
+
+## Method
+
+- Source of truth: the `syntheticSources` map in
+  [internal/frontend/synth_machinery.go](../../internal/frontend/synth_machinery.go)
+  plus the `dedicatedSyntheticStubs` map in
+  [internal/frontend/export.go](../../internal/frontend/export.go), both read at
+  HEAD `59f0a247` (2026-11-07). Keys, source consts and declaring files
+  were extracted mechanically (AST-level key parse + const lookup); the
+  retirement condition for each row was taken from the declaring file's
+  header comment (sentences containing "retir*"), falling back to
+  "needs design" when the header states none.
+- Counts: **130** `syntheticSources` keys + **2** dedicated stubs
+  (`runtime`, `unsafe`) = **132** shadowed import paths. (The review's
+  "140 top-level `synth_*.go` files" counts files, not packages — a
+  different unit: several files carry multiple packages' sources, and
+  a few carry none, e.g. test helpers.)
+- `reflect_m7` is a pseudo-package, not a real import path: the retired
+  `synth_reflect.go` source re-registered under a distinct name so the M7
+  desugaring helpers (`__reflect_taglookup`, `reflectTagPair`) keep
+  resolving. It retires when the M7 desugaring no longer needs those
+  helpers — needs design.
+
+## Finding: no per-package retirement condition is recorded
+
+**All 130 live packages are "needs design".** The synth file headers
+describe the mechanism (embedded real-Go source, overlay import, wire
+emission) and cite design docs, but none states what root-cause fix
+retires that package. The bridge inventory (B-4) requires each synthetic
+to survive only "with a documented, specific, verifiable reason" — the
+reason is documented per file, but the *retirement* side is not. Filling
+in this column is the Phase 3 program's first step; the retired rows
+below are the model for what a filled-in row looks like.
+
