+## How to use this file
+
+1. A Phase 3 lane picks a row, lands the root-cause fix (real stdlib
+   compiles from disk, or a new P3-M4 intrinsic registration), deletes
+   the `syntheticSources` entry (and the `synth_*.go` source when the
+   last package using it goes), and deletes the row here in the same
+   change — docs are part of the change.
+2. The `stdlib-linkdiff` v2 report after the retirement must show the
+   package's targets leaving the skip-list (or gaining registry
+   provision); a retirement that does not move the v2 skip-list did
+   not retire anything the tool can see.
+3. When the last row is deleted, delete the machinery wholesale per
+   bridge-inventory Phase 3 (`syntheticSources` + import overlay +
+   linkname allowlist + intrinsic predicates + `syncop`/`runtimecaller`
+   wire nodes) and delete this file with it.
+
